hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2787","Narrated to us al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān and (narrated to us) Ibn Wahb, who said: And Usāmah (RA) narrated to me.\n\nAlso narrated to us Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā: Ibn Wahb informed us, who said: Usāmah (RA) informed me, that ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ (RA) narrated to him that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (RA) say:\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said, “Every passage in Makkah is a place of sacrifice, and whoever intends to perform ʿUmrah may slaughter his sacrificial animal wherever he wishes in Makkah.”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
